  "accessibilityTree": "- main:\n  - paragraph: About me\n  - paragraph: Product Designer Indonesia\n  - heading \"I design digital products, from the first question to the smallest interaction.\" [level=1]\n  - link \"Let's talk\":\n    - /url: /contact\n  - region \"A little about me\":\n    - heading \"A little about me\" [level=2]\n    - paragraph: I'm Alan, a Product Designer based in Indonesia.\n    - paragraph: My background is in user research, wireframing, and prototyping for web and mobile. I like making sense of a problem, then working through how an interface should look and behave.\n    - paragraph: That curiosity extends to how things are made. I want to understand what happens beyond the mockup, and stay involved as an idea becomes something people can use.\n    - link \"View selected work\":\n      - /url: /#work\n  - figure \"Alan Sahlan Based in Indonesia\":\n    - img \"Alan Sahlan\"\n    - text: Alan Sahlan Based in Indonesia\n  - region \"Where I am now\":\n    - heading \"Where I am now\" [level=2]\n    - paragraph:\n      - link \"CADIT\":\n        - /url: https://www.cadit.com/\n    - paragraph: UI/UX Designer\n    - paragraph:\n      - text: Since\n      - time: October 2025\n    - paragraph: I'm building a component library from the existing design system and creating UI mockups for developers working with international clients.\n    - paragraph: Through CADIT, that work includes Daikin Singapore, Thai Honda, and SP Group Singapore.\n    - link \"Download resume, PDF\":\n      - /url: /resume/alan-sahlan-resume.pdf\n      - text: Download resume PDF\n  - region \"Where I'm heading\":\n    - heading \"Where I'm heading\" [level=2]\n    - paragraph: Design is my starting point. There's more I want to learn.\n    - paragraph: Lately, I've been learning to build interfaces in code. It helps me understand technical constraints, explain design decisions, and refine the details as they take shape.\n    - paragraph: Product design is still at the heart of what I do. Design engineering is a direction I'm growing into, with room to keep exploring.",
